march 8  2022 is that the official release date  for hogwarts legacy people of the  internet retroarch and tour here and we  have yet another hogwarts legacy leak  hit the like button if you've heard that  one before as you all know i'm just a  dad who loves games and the stories they  tell and we've got some juicy juicy  leaks to discuss today now as i alluded  to in the opener this leak pertains to  the game's release date i would also say  it comes from a reliable source but  there's always a butt with these things  right i still don't personally believe  it's actually the release date for the  game in today's video i'll explain the  full leak why i think it is legitimate  but still doesn't give us an accurate  release date and i know you're probably  asking how can the leak be legit but not  have the correct date well let's dive in  this one actually all started back in  september when nvidia suffered a leak  through their cloud gaming subscription  service geforce now the leak was a  database of games but the big deal here  is that it contained a number of  unannounced titles some of which have  ended up coming true such as god of war  for the pc other games in that leak as  apparently coming to geforce now  included other sony titles like eternal  and demon souls as well as completely  unannounced games like a bioshock  remaster titanfall 3 and many others  we've since seen at least part of this  leak turn out to be true as for nvidia's  official statement at the time they  claimed the list was quote used only for  internal tracking and testing close  quote they would also go on to add that  some titles were speculative and not  confirmation nor an announcement of any  game fast forward to now and we have yet  another geforce now leak only this one  includes release dates if you take a  look at this list which i'll link to in  the description below you'll see  potential release dates for games like  crisis gears of war mortal kombat and  yes harry potter universe wait what yeah  for some reason it lists a game being  developed by avalanche software and  published by wb as harry potter universe  now before you get too excited i don't  think this is another harry potter game  i do think it's probably just a  placeholder title they used for hogwarts  legacy who knows maybe this leak is so  old that it's before we even knew the  official title and what i mean by old  leak is even though this just happened  now it very well could be old  information and that leads me back to  the release date the leak shows march 8  2022 as the release for harry potter  universe which i think we can be pretty  sure is hogwarts legacy now as i said in  the beginning i do think this leak is  legit in the sense that it probably is  actually files directly from the geforce  now servers what i don't think it means  is that this is the official release  date for hogwarts legacy first off if  it's releasing in march they would  really need to ramp up the advertising  and marketing for the game very very  soon that's right around four months  away and at this point we haven't heard  a peep about this game for more than a  year now i think the most likely answer  is that this is simply a placeholder  date maybe it was put in there by  someone at nvidia who knows they very  well could have even gotten confirmation  directly from someone at wb or avalanche  but even then it could still just be a  placeholder date until they know the  official one now there's another  interesting angle to this that i think  is going to warrant its own separate  video but yes guys i am well aware of  the toy magazine you heard me write toy  magazine which gave a very tiny update  on hogwarts legacy and it seems like it  may hint at the game releasing after  fantastic beasts 3 which we already know  has been confirmed for april 15th 2022  so if that is the case that would  certainly put another point on the side  of this whole thing with nvidia just  being a placeholder date but more on  that in the next video now maybe there  are some of you out there who don't  follow the gaming industry too closely  so you may wonder what i mean exactly by  placeholder date well this isn't a  practice that's unique to the video game  industry you actually see this with a  lot of different websites the basic idea  is retailers have to prep for the  release of new products well in advance  of the actual launch date this is so  they can have all their back-end systems  set up and ready to go and all they'll  have to change are the details such as  release date or maybe something in the  product description this makes things a  lot easier as they don't have to  scramble to get everything ready at the  last minute they can already have all  this in there pre-loaded and just make a  few tweaks as needed so that's what i  think is going on here i think this is  very likely just a placeholder date for  hogwarts legacy maybe it came from wb  maybe it came from geforce now just  taking a guess to me though the most  interesting aspect of the whole story  would be if the march date was an actual  target date for avalanche at some point  maybe they did actually give that number  to the folks at nvidia at some point in  fact many people hoped back when the  game was delayed from 2022 that maybe  because they had initially announced  2021 it was actually close to release  and they just needed more time to polish  things up as time has gone on throughout  the year of 2021 though and we've gotten  no new information that certainly led  more and more to believe this game won't  see the light of day until very late in  2022 myself included i've said for a  while now i think it's holiday 2022 but  what do you guys think will hogwarts  legacy release on march 8th 2022 let me  know in the comments below as always  thank you all so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon

